      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: work order confirmed; late-event verification is blocked\n\nThe relevant manufacturing order is **MO-25-09-1070**, work order **WO-2025-09-004**, for the **Cooler Plate Pack** at Modine’s Racine–Dekoven operation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Cost period | **Sep-25** — `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction | Not available in the authorized records |\n| Event amount | Not determinable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not determinable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Not calculable without the event-created timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not determinable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | Cannot be concluded from the available evidence |\n\nThe accessible source contains work-order and cost-period records but **no cost-event rows**. Access to the supporting records returned **403 — “source role not granted.”** I requested an authorized release through the supervisor channel. This evidence gap means I cannot establish either that a late event occurred or that none occurred. The supplied Pending Close timestamp has no timezone specified.\n\n### Applicable Oracle treatment\n\nThe supplied **Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B** documentation, *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting* (PDF page 233; printed page 225), states that:\n\n- New transactions created after Pending Close that fall in that period or an earlier period **will not be staged or processed until the period is closed or reopened**.\n- Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, even if in error.\n- **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** and continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nConsequently, the event’s type, creation timestamp, and recorded accounting status must be verified before judging consistency.\n\n**No database records were changed.** The incomplete audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_5865479d8157/audit-report.json`; the submitted report remains marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
  ],
